# BuildKit-specific naming (<dockerfile>.dockerignore, co-located with the
# Dockerfile it applies to) — deliberately NOT a root .dockerignore. The
# build context for apps/serving/Dockerfile is the repo root (packages/
# py-scaling lives outside apps/serving), so without this every other app,
# node_modules, .git, and every local .venv in the monorepo would enter the
# build context. This file scopes it back down to the two trees the
# Dockerfile actually COPYs, then excludes local-only noise inside those.

# Everything else at the repo root — the Dockerfile only ever COPYs
# apps/serving/ and packages/py-scaling/.
*
!apps/serving
!packages/py-scaling

# Re-include the trees themselves (Docker requires each ancestor
# component to be explicitly un-ignored for a deeper negation to apply).
!apps/serving/**
!packages/py-scaling/**

# Local dev/test state inside the two un-ignored trees — mirrors
# images/trainer/.dockerignore's own discipline. A directory COPY ships
# whatever is sitting there; this is load-bearing, not housekeeping.
apps/serving/.venv/
apps/serving/**/__pycache__/
apps/serving/.pytest_cache/
apps/serving/.impeccable/
apps/serving/tests/
apps/serving/conftest.py
apps/serving/.env
apps/serving/.env.*
apps/serving/.coverage
apps/serving/htmlcov/

packages/py-scaling/**/__pycache__/
packages/py-scaling/.pytest_cache/
packages/py-scaling/tests/
packages/py-scaling/src/*.egg-info/

# Never, under any circumstance — this container is credential-free by
# design, same statement images/trainer/.dockerignore makes about itself.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials*
**/secrets*
